WEBVTT

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:41.810
I mean, how can you write your mother and tell her, you know, that her handsome young darling Marine, you know, her hero is, you know, is anti-military, you know?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.460
But I sat down and I wrote her a letter and told her exactly how I felt.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.830
And my mother wrote back and she said that she fully understood and she was happy that I felt that way and that I was anti-military.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:55.940
The way this war is, we aren't really in a pinch, you know, so why should we go out and put our lives down?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.970
That was the alternative of either going to jail or coming in.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.860
service and so I was left with no alternative but to be inducted. I had just gotten out of high

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:14.200
school. I didn't have a job, no prospects for any, no money. The Air Force came along and there I was.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:29.790
Going places, meeting new people, doing exciting things. Ever thought about the Air Force?

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.100
May I call you Airman?

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.180
Oh, yes, Captain.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.320
When I first saw you,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.200
silhouetted in the tower,

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.910
silhouetted by the light from the radar screen,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.100
bringing in that crippled plane,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.340
a wave of confidence welled through me.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.350
And I knew that with you there,

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.480
my F-111 would be a safer place to be.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.320
Oh, Captain, I have a dream.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.880
I have a dream, a big dream,

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.230
a dream of democracy.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.780
Together, together we can help protect the free world from unfair competition

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.890
and ensure that future generations are having a free world to protect.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.110
Yes, sir.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:19.370
In a cold school in old Monterey, I worked very hard and got my MOS.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:26.150
Code of those words say FTA, but what they mean, hey, no one could guess.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.970
Free the Albanian, future teachers of...

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.740
Who would write that on latrines?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.020
Foxtrot, tango, alpha, me

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.260
Tell me, what does it mean?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.660
Just a minute, operator.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.440
Oh, damn, I don't have any change.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.280
Excuse me, private.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.850
Do you have change for a quarter?

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:51.450
Oh, yeah.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:52.390
Yeah!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.640
You do not say yeah to an officer.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.500
An officer is always addressed as sir.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.960
Now, I learned that in basic...

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.500
private and so did you you always address an officer as sir now i'm going to give you one

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.920
more chance and i want to hear that sir loud and clear private do you have change for a quarter

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:25.340
no sir i took one look at my face and ran out barb i said foxtrot tango barb

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.600
I'm gonna get me a watchdog.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.920
What you need a watchdog for, Sarge?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.240
You're surrounded by 250 armed men.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.300
That's where I'm gonna get me a watchdog.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.700
No Vietnamese ever ordered me to fight.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.660
They never flew over my hometown to bomb me.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:48.800
So I have to say,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:54.170
Foxtrot, Tango, Alpha, Friant.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.370
Terrible demonstration going on outside.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.600
Oh, there's always a demonstration going on outside, Pat.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.660
Yeah, but Richard, this one is completely out of control.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:06.400
What are they asking for this time?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.680
Free Angela Davis and all political prisoners,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.610
out of Vietnam now, and draft all government officials.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.530
Well, we have people to take care of that.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.570
They'll do their job, you do your job, and I'll do my job.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.770
Richard, you don't understand. They're storming the White House.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.370
Oh, in that case, I better call out the Third Marines.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.270
You can't, Richard.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:21.610
Why not?

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.750
It is the Third Marines.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:23.030
Oh.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.440
We said, Foxtrot, Tango!

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.500
I went into the army, I thought it was...

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.900
Well, since I had the opportunity to grow up in a free society,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.420
as in America, I owed my country at least two or three years for my life.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.300
So I enlisted and was sent over to Vietnam.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.740
Spent four months there in 1970.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.720
before I was hit three times, was medevaced out to Japan.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.560
At the time of recuperating in Japan,

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.520
I started wondering just what the hell we're in Vietnam for.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.360
When you're taught about the communist monster

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.260
that you're over there to defeat,

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.220
when you get over there and you like see

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.860
when you're going through a ville or something

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.640
to liberate a village, the people hide from you

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.980
and throw rocks and everything else,

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.900
bottles and all that.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:37.860
But when the Viet Cong come to Liberated Village, people go out there yelling, celebrating, holding pictures of Ho Chi Minh.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.780
And, you know, seeing things like this makes you wonder just who this monster really is.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:10.550
And they break your ass, and they ship your ass, and then they shoot your ass, or they

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:29.800
can kiss my ass, kiss my ass, mine, my ass is mine, my ass is mine, my ass, why I feel

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:59.980
I'm feeling super fine, that's why, even when my ass is on the line, and that's why I'm smiling all the time, that's why I'm smiling, because I know they know, I know my ass is mine, might sound a little bit selfish, just like a synonym for selling out, but that depends on what your ass is.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.640
is doing of what your ass is all about if you save your ass by keeping silent about the murder

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:13.960
across the sea if i was vietnamese and you did that i'd say your ass belongs to me but my ass

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:28.160
is mine my ass is mine my ass is mine all the time

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.380
Super fine

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:44.770
Cause I know they know, I know my ass is mine

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:56.520
Had a job, she had a boss

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.180
He had a desk to run her around

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.480
She thought that she could escape that jive by escaping her giant hometown.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:09.440
She sailed clear across the ocean, but baby, now she's really in a mess.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.660
You see, she gave her commanding officer a karate chop in the chest.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:23.790
Now she's telling the whole world she's her own woman, not your girl.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:34.070
She said, I know they know my ass belongs to me

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.960
You know, some say the masses are asses

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:40.540
But I've just come here to tell you they're all wrong

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.000
You see, the masses have just been letting the asses

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Lead them by the nose too long

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.380
We've been busting our ass all evening

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.880
And now I'm saying just for me that my ass belongs to everyone

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.900
Who's fighting to be free

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.980
Yes, my ass is mine, my ass is mine

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:16.400
come on come on if it's my ass i've got to lose where i'll be losing it i will choose

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:27.240
and since the first time i felt free i said i know they know i know my ass belongs to me

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:29.960
because they draft your

