They uniform your ass, and then they drill your ass, I mean they train your ass, then they bust your ass, and they brig your ass, and then they ship your ass, and then they shoot your ass, well they can kiss my ass, they can kiss my ass, and they can kiss my ass, and they can kiss my ass, and they can kiss my ass, and they can kiss my ass, and they can kiss my ass.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:37.720
A tank aircraft carrier USS Coral Sea with 85 planes, 6 million pounds of munitions, 4,500 men.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:44.780
It has dropped more than 850,000 tons of bombs on the people of Indochina.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:53.350
In November 1971, 1,300 of its crew signed a petition to stop their ship from going to Vietnam.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:59.680
You all are not actually on Vietnamese soil. It must be very abstract.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.020
for you. I mean, what the effects of an attack carrier have on the war. What is it that started

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:12.400
you all thinking, and how did you come to understand the role that an attack carrier

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:19.270
plays? I suppose everybody always knows, but they can rationalize anything away. That's

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:23.790
man's, you know, that's the way his mind works. Like, you read the polls and people want us

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:28.510
to get out of Vietnam, and you see the polls getting higher and higher every week, but

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:29.490
yet we aren't out

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.140
You know, and how can you rationalize this?

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.540
You know, we'll be off the coast of Vietnam during Christmas, you know.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:37.020
We'll probably send a strike off during Christmas Day, you know.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.280
So many sick lifers, they'll go down and write Merry Christmas on a bomb, you know.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:47.980
And the chaplain will make, will try and rationalize it, you know, and it's a big joke, but it scares you.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.870
You have to question, and I was always taught to question.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.170
And the service won't let you question because they don't have an answer.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.470
They only have a rule book.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:59.970
And I feel that by my speaking out, you know, if I...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.900
can turn just a couple people to start thinking about it or even even think

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:23.070
about for a couple of seconds I've done what I'm supposed to do here on the

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:27.200
Mekong River Delta where elements of the 101st Airborne tango with a crack North

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.980
Vietnamese 7th Regiment both teams undefeated and untied

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.860
so far this season.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.500
Down on the playing area,

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.360
marshy white paddies surrounded by trees

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.260
with hills in the background.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:40.340
Looking up over those hills,

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.950
here come the Cobra helicopters of the 101st.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:43.990
They're strafing the landing zone

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.190
with 50-caliber machine gun fired.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:45.950
There go the miniguns.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:48.290
And here come the troop-carrying Hueys

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.490
windmilling down into the zone.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.490
It'll be the third brigade of the 101st.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.130
The boys come busting out of the helicopters,

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.970
firing M-16s from the hip as they go,

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:56.510
driving on to set up the line of scrimmage.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.310
There's no sign of the Viet Cong yet,

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.330
no sign of Charlie.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:05.580
Wait a minute, Charlie! Charlie's here, and he's got mortars.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:10.580
I count mortars, one, two, three, four, five rounds of mortar fire, and two make it four.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.520
Huey helicopters down and burning, the rest are up and heading for home.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:17.890
The boys in the 101st have dug in there now.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:20.370
Charlie coming out from behind the mortars with AK-47s.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:23.890
He's heading for the outside of the line, but the boys in the 101st have laid up a wall of grenades,

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.090
small weapons, and machine gun fire.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.710
But Charlie driving on hard, and look at those fireworks,

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.950
the best that American technological know-how can provide.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:31.840
Flashettes, claymores, beehives.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.260
There's Puff the Magic Dragon, 36,000 rounds a minute.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.860
The boys have got four barrel shotguns.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:38.520
And Charlie is slowing down, he's bogged down.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.980
He's stopped, he's stopped, he's stopped.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:40.880
That's the line of scrimmage.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.080
What do you think of the action so far, Red?

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.650
Well, Red, looks like we're in

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.010
for a beautiful game here today.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.280
Both these teams are in tip top condition, boys.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.220
None of them first looking really good out there.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.660
Not that I'm trying to detract from the Viet Cong.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.300
They've had a beautiful season.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.740
I guess you know this, Red.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.020
They are the home team here.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.520
They seem to have a lot of support here

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.600
among the local fans.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.130
Thank you, Red, for that interesting and colorful commentary.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:06.390
Meanwhile, back on the playing field, there's a temporary halt in the action,

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.290
a timeout while the dead and wounded are being dragged from the playing area.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.220
Red, I see Lieutenant Colonel Billy Sluckham on the radio down there,

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.520
and I think he's going to go to the air for the next play.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:16.960
I think he'll look for the bomb.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:21.560
Here they are, from the carrier, USS Enterprise, 4F Phantom jets in formation.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.180
Silver gliding in the sunlight.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.760
They're up and over, down they come.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.020
There go the 20-millimeter cannons.

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:26.960
There go the rocket pods.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:29.920
There go the antipersonal fragmentation bombs, and I count.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.190
12, water buffalo down and kicking.

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:37.230
Again, they're coming in again for a second pass.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:37.930
We'll watch for it.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:38.510
Here they come.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.280
Low coming in.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:40.860
Here it is.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.200
It's Napalm.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:42.540
Wow.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.420
Right on top of the 101st.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.340
There are penalty flags all over the playing area.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.120
They're moving us now into orderly withdrawal.

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:56.360
And lying motionless on the ground is Lieutenant Colonel Billy Slocum.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:59.980
That'll be a fragging penalty for the boys in the 101st.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:03.360
And here's the hotline battlefield tally for the Viet Cong.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.300
117 dead, 212 wounded for the 101st.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.080
